          "guid": "mso7my36p9d6cdmd",
          "message": {
            "text": "A session-probed Windows face is a resolved primary family, not a terminal fallback face, so its requested weight and slope must still go through DirectWrite family matching. The first focused CI run exposed regular Consolas being reused for bold/italic monospace; retaining the declared-family marker lets the existing Chromium-derived cut matcher select Consolas-Bold and Consolas-Italic.",
            "markdown": "A session-probed Windows face is a resolved primary family, not a terminal fallback face, so its requested weight and slope must still go through DirectWrite family matching. The first focused CI run exposed regular Consolas being reused for bold/italic `monospace`; retaining the declared-family marker lets the existing Chromium-derived cut matcher select `Consolas-Bold` and `Consolas-Italic`."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/font-resolution.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 4151,
                  "endLine": 4183,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "function win32PrimaryCutKey(key: string, weight: number, slant: number, stretch: number = 100): string | null {\n  if (WIN32_PRIMARY_CUT_SKIP.has(key)) return null;\n  // A suffix-declared family re-resolves per style even though its key is\n  // dynamic: the suffix pinned one axis, the run still owns the slope.\n  const suffixDecl = win32SuffixDeclaredForKey.get(key);\n  const declaredFamily = declaredFamilyForKey.get(key);\n  // Already-resolved or dynamically-registered faces: the key IS the answer.\n  if (suffixDecl == null && (\n    (key.startsWith(\"sysfb:\") && declaredFamily == null) || key.startsWith(\"winfam:\")\n      || key.startsWith(\"webfont:\") || key.startsWith(\"localalias:\"))) return null;\n\n  const cacheKey = `${key}|${weight}|${slant !== 0 ? 1 : 0}|${stretch}`;\n  const cached = win32PrimaryCutCache.get(cacheKey);\n  if (cached !== undefined) return cached;\n\n  let result: string | null = null;\n  try {\n    // `system-ui` never reaches font matching as a literal in Blink\n    // (`DCHECK_NE(family, kSystemUi)`), so it is asked of the OS.\n    const family = suffixDecl != null\n      ? suffixDecl.family\n      : declaredFamily != null\n        ? declaredFamily\n      : key === \"sf-pro\"\n        ? (resolveSystemUiFamily() ?? fileFamilyNameForKey(key))\n        : fileFamilyNameForKey(key);\n    if (family != null && family !== \"\") {\n      const cut = win32FamilyKey(family, {\n        weight: suffixDecl?.weight ?? weight,\n        slant,\n        fontSize: 16,\n        stretch: suffixDecl?.stretch ?? stretch,\n      });"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
