          "message": {
            "text": "Route provenance must survive the shared SF key. Blink dispatches system-ui to MatchSystemUIFont but author-named SF families to MatchFontFamily; using only sf-pro erased that distinction and leaked CSS-valued axes across routes. The side-band bit avoids duplicating platform tables and is included in cache identity so interleaved calls cannot alias.",
            "markdown": "Route provenance must survive the shared SF key. Blink dispatches system-ui to MatchSystemUIFont but author-named SF families to MatchFontFamily; using only sf-pro erased that distinction and leaked CSS-valued axes across routes. The side-band bit avoids duplicating platform tables and is included in cache identity so interleaved calls cannot alias."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/font-resolution.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 5964,
                  "endLine": 5977,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  // macOS: for a family named by CSS, ask Blink's declared-family style matcher\n  // which CUT the run opens, instead of picking between the two `key` /\n  // `key-bold` slots above. Reads the BASE key, so its answer REPLACES that\n  // routing rather than composing with it (composing would re-weight an\n  // already-re-weighted face). Null leaves the two-slot result standing, which\n  // is the degradation contract for a host with no helper binary.\n  const darwinCut = systemUiPrimary\n    ? null\n    : darwinPrimaryCutKey(key, weight, slant, stretch, declaredFamily);\n  if (darwinCut != null) {\n    effectiveKey = darwinCut.key;\n    // A matched face carrying CoreText's italic trait satisfies the slant with\n    // a real cut; without it the renderer would shear an already-italic face.\n    routedItalicCut = slant !== 0 && darwinCut.italic;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
