          "message": {
            "text": "The reset claimed to drop every process-global font-resolution memo but only cleared the macOS primary-cut cache. Linux and Windows keep equivalent style-sensitive matcher answers, so leaving them warm makes reset behavior platform-asymmetric and can retain stale fontconfig/DirectWrite cuts. The test seeds all three maps on one host and proves the complete zero-size postcondition.",
            "markdown": "The reset claimed to drop every process-global font-resolution memo but only cleared the macOS primary-cut cache. Linux and Windows keep equivalent style-sensitive matcher answers, so leaving them warm makes reset behavior platform-asymmetric and can retain stale fontconfig/DirectWrite cuts. The test seeds all three maps on one host and proves the complete zero-size postcondition."
